# From bigHalf_bus005_dangling.buda
source ../tracks/tracks4top.buda
source tc3a_flat_5x.buda
run_bundler
generate_topologies_for_bundle bus_038 no_hanan_loci
dump_topologies bus_038
check_design topo all
# The original vehicle pinned candidate 20 — the fully-degenerate legacy
# BITRUNK_H whose free-sliding trunk grazed every endpoint block untapped and
# opened all 56 bits at DNUTS.  The generation-time anchoring gate
# (filter_unanchored_bitrunk) now drops that candidate, so the pool is 19 and
# the pin is retired: the flow now demonstrates the HEALTHY default (the gate
# keeps only anchored shapes; planner picks freely, 0/0/0).  Do NOT re-add a
# blind index pin here — under `multi_trunk` (or BUDA_MULTI_TRUNK=1) the pool
# grows and a stale index lands on a degenerate tree again (the 2026-07-30
# default-flip study measured exactly that: 0/56/1 from the re-armed pin).
run_planner
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
check_design
visualize
